/* Ported verbatim from the production site (deeptech_frontend/src/content/master-services-agreement.md). Do not edit wording here without legal review. */
const source: string = "# Master Services Agreement - ASTEAI\n\n**Last Updated:** October 6, 2026 | **Version:** 1.0\n\n---\n\n## 1. Parties and Structure\n\n1.1 This Master Services Agreement (\"MSA\") is between **Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd.**, a company incorporated in India with its registered office in Chennai, Tamil Nadu, operating the ASTEAI platform (\"ASTEAI\"), and the business that signs or accepts an Order Form referencing this MSA (\"Customer\").\n\n1.2 It applies to business and enterprise use of ASTEAI, including ASTEAI Hire subscriptions, enterprise workspaces, and expert-engagement services bought by an organisation. Individual users are governed by the Terms and Conditions alone.\n\n1.3 **Order of precedence.** If documents conflict, they apply in this order:\n1. the Order Form, but only for commercial terms (services, fees, term, service levels) expressly stated in it;\n2. the Data Processing Agreement (\"DPA\"), for the processing of personal data;\n3. this MSA;\n4. the Terms and Conditions and other platform policies.\n\n1.4 The DPA at https://asteai.com/dpa is incorporated into this MSA.\n\n## 2. Services\n\n2.1 ASTEAI will provide the services described in each Order Form or chosen in the Customer's plan in the product (\"Services\"), in accordance with this MSA and with reasonable skill and care.\n\n2.2 ASTEAI may improve or change the Services. It will not materially reduce the core functionality of a paid subscription during a paid term, and will give at least 30 days' notice of any material change that adversely affects the Customer.\n\n2.3 **Service levels.** Any uptime commitment, support response time, or service credit applies only if it is stated in the Order Form. Otherwise ASTEAI will use commercially reasonable efforts to keep the Services available, excluding planned maintenance and events outside its reasonable control.\n\n2.4 **Expert services.** Where the Customer engages experts through the platform, the expert is an independent contractor. The engagement contract, escrow, and dispute process in the Terms and Conditions apply to that work.\n\n## 3. Customer Responsibilities\n\n3.1 The Customer is responsible for its authorised users, keeping credentials secure, and all activity under its account.\n\n3.2 The Customer will use the Services lawfully. In particular it must:\n- give candidates and other individuals any notice required by law and obtain any required consent before their data is processed through the Services;\n- not upload sensitive personal data that the Services do not need (see Annex 1 of the DPA);\n- make its own hiring and engagement decisions. AI scores, rankings, summaries, and recommendations are decision-support tools, may be inaccurate, and must be reviewed by a human before any decision that significantly affects an individual;\n- comply with the Acceptable Use rules in the Terms and Conditions.\n\n## 4. Fees and Payment\n\n4.1 The Customer will pay the fees in the Order Form or, if there is none, the plan prices published at the time of purchase.\n\n4.2 Fees are exclusive of GST and other taxes, which the Customer will pay in addition. If the Customer must withhold tax, it will provide the withholding certificate so ASTEAI can claim credit.\n\n4.3 Unless the Order Form says otherwise, subscription fees are billed in advance for each billing cycle, and invoices are payable within **15 days** of the invoice date.\n\n4.4 ASTEAI may suspend the Services, after giving at least 10 days' written notice, if undisputed fees are more than 30 days overdue.\n\n4.5 Fees are non-refundable except as stated in this MSA, the DPA, the Refund Policy, or the Cancellation Policy.\n\n4.6 ASTEAI may change prices for a renewal term by giving at least 30 days' notice before the renewal date.\n\n## 5. Term and Termination\n\n5.1 This MSA continues while any Order Form or paid subscription is in effect.\n\n5.2 Each subscription runs for the term in its Order Form or plan and, unless the Order Form says otherwise, renews automatically for the same period unless either party cancels before the renewal date. Downgrades and cancellations take effect at the end of the current billing cycle.\n\n5.3 Either party may terminate this MSA or an Order Form by written notice if the other party:\n- materially breaches it and does not cure the breach within 30 days of notice; or\n- becomes insolvent, enters liquidation, or has a receiver or administrator appointed.\n\n5.4 If the Customer terminates for ASTEAI's uncured material breach, ASTEAI will refund prepaid fees for the unused part of the term.\n\n5.5 On termination, the Customer may export its data for 30 days, after which ASTEAI will delete it as set out in Section 11 of the DPA. Sections 4 (for fees accrued), 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, and 12 survive termination.\n\n## 6. Confidentiality\n\n6.1 \"Confidential Information\" means non-public information disclosed by one party to the other that is marked confidential or that a reasonable person would treat as confidential. It includes Customer Data, ASTEAI's non-public product information, and the terms of any Order Form.\n\n6.2 The receiving party will use Confidential Information only to perform or receive the Services, protect it with at least reasonable care, and disclose it only to employees, contractors, and advisers who need to know it and are bound by equivalent confidentiality obligations.\n\n6.3 These obligations do not apply to information that is or becomes public through no fault of the receiving party, was already known to it, was independently developed, or was lawfully received from a third party. A party may disclose Confidential Information when required by law, after giving the other party prompt notice where lawful.\n\n6.4 Confidentiality obligations last for the term and 3 years afterwards, and indefinitely for trade secrets and personal data.\n\n## 7. Data Protection and Security\n\n7.1 \"Customer Data\" means data the Customer or its users submit to the Services, or that ASTEAI collects for the Customer through the Services. As between the parties, the Customer owns Customer Data.\n\n7.2 ASTEAI processes personal data within Customer Data as the Customer's processor under the DPA.\n\n7.3 ASTEAI maintains an Information Security Management System certified to ISO/IEC 27001:2022 and the security measures described in Annex 2 of the DPA. On request, ASTEAI will provide a copy of its certificate and complete a reasonable security questionnaire once per year.\n\n7.4 ASTEAI will not use Customer Data to train AI models made available to other customers, and will not sell Customer Data.\n\n## 8. Intellectual Property\n\n8.1 ASTEAI and its licensors own the Services, the platform, its software, models, and documentation, and all improvements to them. Except for the rights expressly granted, no rights are transferred.\n\n8.2 Subject to payment, ASTEAI grants the Customer a non-exclusive, non-transferable right for its authorised users to use the Services during the term for its internal business purposes.\n\n8.3 The Customer grants ASTEAI a limited licence to host, process, and display Customer Data as needed to provide, secure, and support the Services.\n\n8.4 ASTEAI may use aggregated, de-identified data that does not identify the Customer or any individual to operate and improve the Services.\n\n8.5 The Customer may give feedback about the Services. ASTEAI may use it freely and without obligation.\n\n8.6 Ownership of work product created by experts for the Customer is governed by the engagement contract and Section 7.4 of the Terms and Conditions.\n\n## 9. Warranties and Disclaimers\n\n9.1 Each party warrants that it has authority to enter this MSA.\n\n9.2 ASTEAI warrants that it will provide the Services materially in accordance with their documentation. If it does not, the Customer's remedy is for ASTEAI to correct the issue or, if it cannot within a reasonable time, for the Customer to terminate the affected Services and receive a pro-rata refund of prepaid fees.\n\n9.3 Except as stated in this MSA, the Services are provided \"as is\". To the extent permitted by law, ASTEAI disclaims all other warranties, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. ASTEAI does not warrant that AI outputs, candidate assessments, or expert evaluations are accurate or complete, or that any candidate or expert will perform as predicted.\n\n## 10. Indemnities\n\n10.1 **By ASTEAI.** ASTEAI will defend the Customer against third-party claims that the Services, as provided by ASTEAI, infringe that third party's intellectual property rights, and will pay damages finally awarded or agreed in settlement. This does not apply to claims arising from Customer Data, from combining the Services with things ASTEAI did not provide, or from modifications ASTEAI did not make.\n\n10.2 **By the Customer.** The Customer will defend ASTEAI against third-party claims arising from Customer Data, from the Customer's breach of Section 3.2, or from the Customer's hiring or engagement decisions, and will pay damages finally awarded or agreed in settlement.\n\n10.3 The indemnified party must notify the indemnifying party promptly, give it sole control of the defence and settlement (no settlement may impose liability on the indemnified party without its consent), and provide reasonable cooperation.\n\n## 11. Limitation of Liability\n\n11.1 Neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential losses, or for loss of profits, revenue, goodwill, or data (other than the cost of restoring data from backups), even if advised of the possibility.\n\n11.2 Each party's total liability arising out of or relating to this MSA is limited to the **fees paid and payable by the Customer in the 12 months** before the event giving rise to the claim.\n\n11.3 The limits in Sections 11.1 and 11.2 do not apply to:\n- the Customer's obligation to pay fees;\n- a party's indemnity obligations under Section 10;\n- breach of Section 6 (Confidentiality), except as it relates to Customer Data, which is covered by Section 11.4;\n- fraud, gross negligence, or wilful misconduct;\n- any liability that cannot be limited by law.\n\n11.4 For breach of Section 7 or the DPA, ASTEAI's total liability is limited to **twice** the amount in Section 11.2.\n\n## 12. General\n\n12.1 **Governing law and disputes.** This MSA is governed by the laws of India. The parties will first try to resolve any dispute through good-faith discussion between senior representatives for 30 days. Unresolved disputes will be finally resolved by arbitration under the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, by a sole arbitrator appointed by agreement or, failing agreement, under that Act. The seat of arbitration is Chennai, Tamil Nadu, and the language is English. Subject to this, the courts at Chennai have exclusive jurisdiction. Either party may seek urgent interim relief from a competent court.\n\n12.2 **Insurance.** ASTEAI maintains insurance appropriate to its business and will provide a certificate of insurance on reasonable request.\n\n12.3 **Force majeure.** Neither party is liable for delay or failure caused by events beyond its reasonable control, other than payment obligations.\n\n12.4 **Assignment.** Neither party may assign this MSA without the other's consent, except to a successor in a merger, acquisition, or sale of substantially all of its relevant assets, with notice to the other party.\n\n12.5 **Subcontracting.** ASTEAI may use subcontractors and Sub-processors (as set out in the DPA) and remains responsible for them.\n\n12.6 **Publicity.** Neither party may use the other's name or logo in marketing without prior written consent.\n\n12.7 **Notices.** Legal notices must be in writing and sent by email with a copy by courier to the addresses in the Order Form. ASTEAI's notice address is legal@asteai.com, Startrit Infratech Pvt. Ltd., Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India - 600095.\n\n12.8 **Entire agreement.** This MSA, the DPA, and the Order Forms are the entire agreement on their subject matter. Terms in a Customer purchase order or vendor portal do not apply, even if accepted. Amendments must be in writing and signed by both parties, or accepted through an Order Form.\n\n12.9 **Other.** If a provision is unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. Failure to enforce a right is not a waiver. The parties are independent contractors. There are no third-party beneficiaries.\n\n---\n\n**Contact for enterprise agreements:** legal@asteai.com\n";
